WEBVTT

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.500
-(MARLIN GROANS)
-(NEMO SIGHS)

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.220
Or on top of quarantine.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.980
SIGOURNEY: The baby otter talk
is beginning now.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:13.540
Why, thanks, Sigourney Weaver.
Hey, who wants to learn about otters?

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.740
(CHILDREN CHEERING)

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.060
DORY: Looking for the world's
most powerful pair of glasses.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.540
(GASPS) Otters!

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.820
-Welcome, it's a huge cuddle party!
-Cuddle party! I'm in!

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.740
Where are we?
Are we close to Open Ocean?

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.260
Uh, yes. I think-- Well, I don't know.
But I saw that other sign so--

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.420
What? What other sign?

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.900
The world's most powerful
pair of glasses.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.780
What? What are you talking about?
Why would we follow that sign?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.100
Well, because I remembered it.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.980
No. That wasn't the plan. Ow!

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.980
All right, that's it!
You have wasted my time!

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.180
-Wait. No.
-That transport truck leaves at dawn...

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.140
and I'm not missing it,
so give me your tag.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.740
Wait. No, I remembered that sign.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.500
-So?
-So I'm remembering more...

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.940
and more and I feel like my memory's
getting better. I think we should--

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.780
No! Your memory is not working.
You can't remember anything.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.580
It's probably how you lost your family
in the first place!

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.700
(GASPS)

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.340
All right, look, let's just take it down
a notch. Just give me the tag and--

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.780
You know something, for a guy
with three hearts you're not very nice.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.140
Three hearts? What are you talking
about? I don't have three hearts.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.420
-Yes, you do.
-I don't!

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.300
-You do!
-Don't!

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.580
-Do!
-Stop saying that!

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.820
Fun fact- the octopus has three hearts.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.100
Two pump blood to the gills
while the third pumps...

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.580
-blood throughout the body.
-Wait!

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:22.940
Whoa! (SCREAMING)

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.500
You know, someone with three hearts
shouldn't be so mean.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.060
And it's mean to say that
I would lose someone I love!

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.540
I did not lose them! Hank?

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.500
Hank? Hank?

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.980
-Han-s.
-No. Not Hans. I'm looking for Hank.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.300
-Han-s.
-Hank. With a "k." Hank.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.620
-Hands!
-Hands? Oh, oh, oh, hands!

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:48.700
(SCREAMS)

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.620
(SCREAMS)

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.260
-Hank! Hank?
-(GROANING)

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.380
My arm!

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.140
Hank!

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.660
(CHILDREN CHATTERING)

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.660
(SCREAMS) Where are you? Hank!

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:02.460
Oh! Ahh! Can you please help me?
I'm looking for--

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.740
(BOTH SCREAMING)

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.980
Please help me. I've lost
my friend Frank. I'm sorry, not Frank.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.260
You're in my space! (SCREAMS)

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.700
He's an octopus. No, septo--
Septopus. That's right.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.460
He's a septopus. Septopus.
Septopus. Septopus. (GASPS)

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.540
One, two, three, four, five, six, s--
Septopus! He's camouflaged!

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.940
(PANTING)

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.340
(YELPS)

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.940
Hank. Come on, Hank!
Let's get out of here.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.700
-(GRUNTING)
-Dory, what are you doing?

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.580
(STAMMERING) Hank!
What's the plan?

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.860
The plan is I'm gonna stay here forever.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.300
Okay. Good plan.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.540
(SCREAMING)

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.900
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Hank. I'm sorry.
I can't remember right. (GASPS)

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.660
-Sweetie. Sweetie.
-Oh, watch out, kelpcake.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.020
Oh, watch where you're going.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.260
I'm sorry, Daddy.
I'm sorry I can't remember right.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:51.860
Oh, sweetie.
Sweetie, you don't need to be sorry.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.460
You know what you need to do?
Just keep swimming.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.620
Yeah.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.940
And I bet you can remember
that because we're just--

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.380
Um...

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:03.900
We're gonna sing a song about it.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.900
♪ Just keep swimming
Just keep swimming

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.620
BOTH: ♪ Just keep swimming
Swimming, swimming

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.660
♪ What do we do?
We swim

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.740
♪ Swim, swim, swim
We swim

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.500
-♪ We swim, swim, swim
-DORY: ♪ Just keep swimming ♪

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.580
(LAUGHS)

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.900
(LAUGHING)

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.180
(GASPS) My parents
taught me that song!

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.660
We sang it as a family.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.260
All this time I thought I made it up!

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.060
-What song?
-Just keep swimming.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.260
Hank, we've just got to keep swimming.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.700
What? No way! Listen to me,
it's too dangerous to move.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.660
No, you listen to me. I know
you're scared, but you can't give up.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.820
Follow me.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.460
♪ Just keep swimming
Just keep swimming

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.500
(SCREAMS)

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.020
♪ My mom wrote
this song for me

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.060
(BOTH SCREAM)

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.940
♪ It's gonna get us out of here ♪

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.500
Sing with me, Hank. Come on.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.500
(GASPS) I'm coming, Mommy.
I'm coming, Daddy!

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.260
-We're gonna be okay.
-Stop!

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.820
-Huh?
-Turn back.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.140
Turn back!

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.180
ALL: You're headed
right for Poker's Cove.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.140
Poker's Cove.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.980
-Poker's Cove?
-Incoming!

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.100
(GRUNTING)

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.620
-(SCREAMS)
-Stop it!

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.300
CHILDREN: Oh, what is this?

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.620
(CHILDREN SCREAMING)

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.300
HANK: Sorry.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.780
DORY: That's okay. Everybody does it.
Nothing to be ashamed of.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.740
Hank? Oh, Hank. There you are.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:28.060
Wow. You got us out of there.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.900
Huh. I did.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.900
I got us out of there.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.020
I mean, technically
you also got us in there.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.180
But if you hadn't I'm not sure
we would have gotten here.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.700
Echolocation. Echolocation!

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:49.300
The world's most powerful pair
of glasses. We found it!

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.540
No. You found that.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:54.780
(GASPS)

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.660
SIGOURNEY ON SPEAKERS:
Welcome to the Open Ocean.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:01.740
Home.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:09.020
MARLIN: Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo, ooo-roo.
Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.100
Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo, ooo-roo!

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.940
Dad, stop. She's not coming back.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.580
She might. Ooo-roo, ooo-roo!

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.780
Dad! You made her feel like
she couldn't do it.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.860
You're not talking about Becky, are you?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.700
(SIGHS)

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.580
I miss Dory.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.460
Me too.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.540
(GRUNTING)

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.060
(SIGHS)

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:38.460
The truth is,
I'm just so worried about her.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.060
She's the one who should be worried
about us.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.700
Well, she would definitely have an idea
of what to do if she were here.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.060
I don't know how she does that.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:51.060
I don't think she knows, Dad.
She just does.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.900
Well, then we'll just have to think.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.580
-What would Dory do?
-What would Dory do?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.660
Yeah! What would Dory do?

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:03.100
She would assess her situation,
and then she'd evaluate...

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.980
then she would analyze her options--

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.740
Dad, that's "what would Marlin do."

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.260
Right, that's what I would do.
She wouldn't even think twice.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.500
She would just look at the first thing
she sees and--

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.220
-(GASPS)
-(CHILDREN LAUGHING)

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:24.740
(SIGHS)

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.420
Dory would do it.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:29.340
Mmm.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.340
-Nemo, hold on to me.
-(BOTH INHALE SHARPLY)

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:33.420
Whoa!

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:34.780
(MARLIN SCREAMING)

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.180
NEMO: Whoo-hoo!

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.500
Hey, it's working! Whoa!

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:42.100
(BOTH GASPING)

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.940
Just keep gasping.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.700
(BOTH SCREAMING)

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.820
(GASPS)

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.500
-Are you okay?
-Yeah! What would Dory do now?

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:57.700
Who's Dory?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.140
Oh boy. Are we happy to see you.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.540
Happy to see me? I'm happy to see you!

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:06.340
I haven't had anyone to talk to in years.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:08.180
Years? Wow.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.380
Unfortunately we can't stay long.
We have to go because--

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.180
Now why would you want to go?
You just landed.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:16.300
Stay a while. Tell me all about yourself.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.180
I would love to, but my son and I
have to get to quarantine, so--

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:21.380
-Wonderful thing to have a son.
-Yeah it is.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.660
Of course I don't have a family.
I dated a nice scallop for a while.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.660
-That's fascinating, but--
-But scallops have eyes.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.860
And she was looking for something
different. I'm kidding!

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:30.980
Well, not about scallops having eyes.
They do.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.420
And they see into your soul
and they break your heart.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.900
Oh, Shelley! Why? Why?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.420
Now what would Dory do?

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.220
SIGOURNEY ON SPEAKERS:
Come with us as we explore

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:46.180
the mysterious world
of the Open Ocean.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.340
-Okay, Hank, follow me.
-You're in a cup.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:51.940
Right. I'll follow you then.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:54.740
(HANK GRUNTS)

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.860
(GRUNTS)

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:07.180
-Wait.
-An octopus has three hearts.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.580
-Huh. That's a fun fact.
-(GROANS)

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.260
(GRUNTING)

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:13.860
(PANTING)

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:19.060
(WHISTLING)

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.300
DORY: We're here.
This is really happening.

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:23.460
HANK: Sh!

